+        // NetSyncClient.Update, every Update of a client (right after ObserveHostDialog: GuestTick(fld, LastHostField)) and of the selftest
+        // role (right after ServiceSpeed, before its scope returns: GuestTick(fld, -1)), on a field or not: the cache's verdict, and its clear
+        // when it no longer stands. fldMapNo flips inside the MAPJUMP tick, so this clears a cache for the field my copy left before that
+        // load's landing hook, in either Unity order. C reads only fldMapNo (the caller's) and the cache.
+        // [ff9mapkit netsync s164] THE ARRIVAL GUARD: ArriveTick runs FIRST, before the cache's return (its own try, never throws): the late
+        // bench write, the episode's end and the guard's spend -- it also reads my user control, NetSyncStepOut.Active / HarnessWhy and
+        // Time.frameCount (its own doc block owns the detail).
+        internal static void GuestTick(Int32 myField, Int32 hostLane)
+        {
